From: hippoley
Subject: [PATCH PROPOSAL] doctor: keep disk-space lint on operator source env

Current-main proposal for OpenClaw PR #154829.

This patch is intentionally narrow:
- keep ordinary no-argument disk-space callers unchanged;
- allow structured findings to resolve from an explicit env;
- pass Doctor health-check ctx.env at the registration boundary;
- do not mutate process.env or weaken plugin-state isolation.

